/// Given an array of signed 8-bit integers `s`, returns a new array of equal length,
/// where every consecutive block of three elements (starting from the beginning)
/// is cyclically shifted left by one position.
///
/// To elaborate:
/// - Let L be the largest multiple of 3 ≤ s.len(), i.e., L = s.len() - (s.len() % 3).
/// - For each i in [0, L):
///   - if i % 3 == 0, result[i] = s[i + 1]
///   - if i % 3 == 1, result[i] = s[i + 1]
///   - if i % 3 == 2, result[i] = s[i - 2]
/// - For i in [L, s.len()), result[i] = s[i].
///
